# Draft workflow — accompaniment document

> **Sibling rule**: `.cursor/rules/client-deliverables.mdc` (content restrictions).
> This rule covers **composition**; the other covers **what cannot appear**.
> Align both if you change either.

## Source vs artifact

- `.md` files in this folder are **editable sources** for the accompaniment document.
- `*-draft.docx` is a **generated artifact** from Pandoc; do not hand-edit — change the `.md` and regenerate.
- The `- draft` suffix on `.docx` is intentional: the final client deliverable usually gets manual polish in Google Docs on top of the corporate template.

## Hierarchical numbering

The final `.docx` combines several `.md` files — numbering must be continuous:

- Main `.md`: sections 1–4 (`# 1. Motivo`, `# 2. Etapa`, `# 3. Detalle`,
  `# 4. Anexos técnicos`).
- Annex A: `# 5. Anexo A — …` with `## 5.1`, `## 5.2`…
- Annex B: `# 6. Anexo B — …` with `## 6.1`, `## 6.2`…
- Annex C: `# 7. Anexo C — …` with `## 7.1`, `## 7.2`…

When adding annex D → section 8, etc., and update cross-references in the main `.md`.

## Hard gate before regenerating `.docx`

**Required:** run the internal-reference linter on source `.md` files and get **empty** output. Fix any hits and repeat.

```bash
cd "docs/draft" && grep -niE \
  "docs/|\.cursor|backlog/|architecture-gaps-and-questions|ARCHITECTURE\.md|SPEC\.md|archimate-{{CLIENT_SLUG}}|archi-server|transcripts/|transcripci|\.mdc|\btask-[0-9]|\bCursor\b" \
  *.md
```

Also do a **semantic review** (not grep-able):

- Internal-only consulting meetings without the client cited by name/context? Reword.
- Ambiguous phrases like “official list” without saying **client-provided**? Clarify.
- Meeting dates without making clear they are **with the client**? Add context.

Only regenerate after both pass.

## Prerequisite (one-time)

Install Pandoc for your OS (e.g. `brew install pandoc` on macOS, package managers on Linux, installer on Windows).

Copy the corporate template (`{{CORPORATE_DOCX_TEMPLATE_NAME}}`) into `docs/templates/`
from {{CONSULTANCY_NAME}}’s template repo or corporate storage.

## Canonical Pandoc command

```bash
cd "docs/draft" && pandoc \
  "{{DOC_TITLE_PREFIX}} - [Nombre-Entregable].md" \
  "{{DOC_TITLE_PREFIX}} - [Nombre-Entregable] - Notas [Tema-A].md" \
  -o "{{DOC_TITLE_PREFIX}} - [Nombre-Entregable] - draft.docx" \
  --reference-doc="../../templates/{{CORPORATE_DOCX_TEMPLATE_NAME}}" \
  --lua-filter="remove-bookmarks.lua"
```

> Replace `[Nombre-Entregable]` and `[Tema-A]` with real names.
> Pandoc concatenates `.md` in **command order** for section order.

`--lua-filter=remove-bookmarks.lua` avoids Google Docs showing one “bookmark” chip per heading.

## Adding a new annex

1. Create `{{DOC_TITLE_PREFIX}} - [Nombre-Entregable] - Notas [Tema-N].md` in this folder.
2. Give the `# H1` the next number (e.g. `# 8. Anexo D — …`), subsections `## 8.1`, etc.
3. Reference the annex from section 4 of the main `.md`.
4. Append it to the Pandoc command in numeric order.
5. Pass hard gate and regenerate `.docx`.
6. Update the “Current files” table in `docs/deliverables/README.md`.

## Manual steps after regenerating draft

1. Open a Google Docs copy of the corporate template; rename with deliverable + version (e.g. "{{CLIENT_DISPLAY_NAME}} — {{INITIATIVE_DISPLAY_NAME}} —
   [Nombre-Entregable] — v1.0").
2. Fill cover (title/subtitle) by hand.
3. Open this folder’s `.docx` in Google Docs, select from "1. Motivo del trabajo" to the end, copy.
4. Paste into the template between the TOC and **Historial de Versiones**.
5. Update TOC (Update table of contents).
6. Add a row to **Historial de Versiones**.
